# The step of axpy_1_entry: axpy_step_1 on an array y that the program supplies, which passes
# through guard before it is added (rule R3; milestone2.md, "Arrays that the program fills").
# Its bound, relative to the terms |a x| + |y|, from those of mul_1_1 and add_1_1, eps = u/(1+u):
#   |z - (a x + y)| <= eps (2 + eps) |a x| + eps |y| + (1 + eps) eta/2,
# and eps (2 + eps) = u (2 + 3u)/(1 + u)^2, (1 + eps)/2 = (1 + 2u)/(2 + 2u) <= 2/3.
kernel:        axpy_entry_step_1
input:         a
input:         x
input:         y
output:        z
value:         a*x+y
ensures:       error z T c=(2+3*u)/((1+u)*(1+u)) k=1 t=2/3
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/MapSteps.v axpy_entry_step_1_correct
source:        the step of axpy (milestone2.md, "sum, dot, axpy, convolution"): the product, then the sum, mul_1_1 then add_1_1 on the guarded y
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes

p  = mul_1_1(a, x)
gy = guard(y)
z  = add_1_1(p, gy)
